# Device: no console window

**Rule:** Unless the human asked for testing/debug (`--selftest`, `--smoke-backtest`, or `-KeepConsole`), the device GUI must never show a console. Closing a console must never kill the app.

## Do

- Launch with `.\scripts\packaging\launch-device.ps1` (pythonw / frozen / MSI, `CreateNoWindow`)
- Or Start Menu / Desktop / MSI shortcuts (`launch-device.vbs` → windowed `TrendAlgoDevice.exe`)
- Autostart already prefers `pythonw.exe` (`autostart.default_command`)

## Do not

- `Start-Process uv run python -m trendalgo.device` for a normal GUI relaunch
- `uv run python -m trendalgo.device` as the product launch path (console `python.exe` owns a console; closing it kills the process)
- Attach a console for GUI runs

## Testing only

- `.\scripts\packaging\launch-device.ps1 -KeepConsole`
- `TRENDALGO_KEEP_CONSOLE=1` (skips `FreeConsole` safety net in `console_detach.py`)
- `--selftest` / `--smoke-backtest` (may `AllocConsole` on frozen builds)
